1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,040
Why does a ship float?

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,140
Why does a spinning top stay up?

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:09,540
Children never stop asking why.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:20,029
İDÜ Lab turns every “why” into an experiment your child can run, and you can share.

5
00:00:28,775 --> 00:00:30,415
First, the practical part.

6
00:00:30,475 --> 00:00:32,015
İDÜ Lab is free.

7
00:00:32,075 --> 00:00:38,015
It runs in the browser on phones, tablets and computers, with nothing to install.

8
00:00:38,075 --> 00:00:44,815
Add it to your home screen, and it opens like an app: no app store needed.

9
00:00:44,875 --> 00:00:50,215
The first three levels of every game are open without an account.

10
00:00:50,275 --> 00:00:58,673
From level four on, a free account saves your child’s progress.

11
00:00:59,283 --> 00:01:00,923
Safety comes first.

12
00:01:00,983 --> 00:01:08,923
A child under thirteen gets an account only together with a parent or guardian, using the guardian’s e-mail address.

13
00:01:08,983 --> 00:01:15,323
Each child needs their own account, so progress and classes never get mixed up.

14
00:01:15,383 --> 00:01:22,923
Account data stays on Izmir Demokrasi University’s own server, and passwords are stored as salted hashes.

15
00:01:22,983 --> 00:01:29,182
And you can delete the account at any time.

16
00:01:29,792 --> 00:01:32,032
Two questions parents often ask.

17
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:34,832
Is my child’s play used for research?

18
00:01:34,892 --> 00:01:41,232
Research questions never appear in primary-school games or for under-13s, and taking part is voluntary.

19
00:01:41,292 --> 00:01:43,032
And what about AI?

20
00:01:43,092 --> 00:01:50,232
Every game screen asks AI assistants to give hints only, never solutions.

21
00:01:50,292 --> 00:01:59,690
Because the point is for your child to run the experiment and discover why.

22
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:02,740
The best part? You can play together.

23
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:07,840
Ask your child, “What do you predict?” before they press Test.

24
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:12,540
Celebrate the wrong guesses: that’s how scientists learn.

25
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:18,340
Read their notebook together, and share a discovery card with the family.

26
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:30,198
Not sure where to start? Kuark suggests games from your child’s age, grade and interests, and explains why.

27
00:02:30,708 --> 00:02:32,048
Being a parent at İDÜ Lab means this:

28
00:02:32,108 --> 00:02:34,048
You don’t need all the answers.

29
00:02:34,108 --> 00:02:38,048
Just ask: what do you think will happen?

30
00:02:38,108 --> 00:02:46,470
Then discover it together.

